---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="Word2Vec Lab | Ravikumar Buragapu"
			description="A from-scratch NumPy skip-gram experiment with negative sampling, analogy evaluation, and embedding visualization."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<p>EMBEDDINGS · WORD2VEC · REPRESENTATION EVALUATION</p>
			<h1>Word2Vec Lab</h1>
			<p>
				Do word analogies such as “king − man + woman = queen”
				hold in a corpus, and how sensitive are they to embedding
				dimension, context window, and negative sampling?
			</p>

			<section aria-labelledby="measures">
				<h2 id="measures">Inspect embedding geometry</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>NumPy skip-gram with negative sampling and a 27-configuration parameter sweep.</li>
					<li>Analogy accuracy with explicit OOV coverage and category-level results.</li>
					<li>Hand-labeled nearest-neighbor precision@k and per-run training time.</li>
					<li>Optional GloVe and FastText baselines and category-colored t-SNE.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					The included corpus and labels are illustrative fixtures,
					not private papers, a standard benchmark, or evidence that
					a particular analogy holds. Use an authorized corpus and
					review your own evaluation pairs.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="run">
				<h2 id="run">Run the experiment</h2>
				<pre><code>cd word2vec-lab
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
pytest
word2vec-lab
# Optional FastText and t-SNE:
pip install -e ".[fasttext,viz]"
word2vec-lab --baselines --visualize</code></pre>
				<p>
					<a href="https://github.com/buragapuravi/ravikumarburagapu.com/tree/main/word2vec-lab"
						>Read the project README</a
					>
					·
					<a href="/projects/learned-ann">Explore Learned ANN Index</a>
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
